{{Quote|I look at the state of the Empire and think, 'How many Super Star Destroyers could we have made with the resources we threw into Tarkin's folly?'|[[Grand General]] [[Cassio Tagge]], referring to the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]|<ref name="Darth Vader (2015) 2">[[Darth Vader (2015) 2|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 2]]</ref>}}
The '''''Executor''-class Star Dreadnought''', also known as the '''''Executor''-class Super Star Destroyer''', officially identified during production as the '''''Super''-class Star Destroyer''', and simply as the '''Super Star Destroyer class''', the '''Super Star Destroyer''' and '''Super Class''', designed by [[Lira Wessex]] were some of the largest and most powerful [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[starship]]s ever created.<ref name="SSD DB" /> Along with other classes of massive Imperial [[capital ship]]s,<ref name="CL 2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> they were also referred to as [[Super Star Destroyer]]s,<ref name="SSD DB" /> although they were technically classified as [[Star Dreadnought]]s. The most distinguished Super [[Star Destroyer]] was the ''[[Executor]]'', [[flagship]] of the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]], [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].<ref name="UltimateSW" />

==Description==
===Overview===
{{Quote|I haven't seen anything that big since the Death Star.|Luke Skywalker reacts to the ''Executor'' during the Battle of Mako-Ta|<ref name="Star Wars 50">[[Star Wars (2015) 50|''Star Wars'' (2015) 50]]</ref>}}
[[File:SSD-Assault-Prototype.png|thumb|right|300px|A prototype ''Executor''-class dreadnought under construction.]]
Vessels of the ''Executor''-class Dreadnought line<ref name="UltimateSW" /> measured at 19,000 [[meter]]s in length,<ref name="Starfighters" /> and utilizing its thirteen [[Executor-50.x engine]]s,<ref name="BMF 27" /> could reach speeds of 100 [[Kilometer per hour|kilometers per hour]]. These [[starship]]s had a crew of 280,784, and could carry 38,000 troops and support staff. The ''Executor''-class possessed long range [[sensor]]s, and had consumables for 6 years. The ''Executor''-class Star Dreadnought possessed a [[Navigation computer|navicomputer]], and had a primary hyperdrive of Class 1, with a backup of Class 10.<ref name="Starships and Speeders">''[[Starships and Speeders]]''</ref> They possessed a [[titanium]]-reinforced [[hull]]<ref name="Starfighters" /> made of [[alusteel]], intended to reflect the design of the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]],<ref name="BMF 27" /> and their [[Bridge (starship)|bridges]] had [[deflector shield]]s and communication domes.<ref name="UltimateSWN">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> The main bridge also resembles a normal ISD bridge, and the bridge also sticks out. Unlike the ISD, the hull is painted black, with a much more pronounced dagger shape. Most of the ship's top is flat, with the main superstructure being a darker shade of gray and resembling a city. Vessels of the ''Executor''-class also had at least one ventral [[hangar]] bay<ref name="UltimateSW" /> and [[escape pod]]s.<ref name="Empire's End" />

The ''Executor''-class's bridge was 285 meters wide and contained shield generators, briefing rooms, and escape pods. However, it was relatively exposed, making it vulnerable to enemy attack.<ref name="CL 2016" />

===Armament===
The ''Executor''-class Dreadnought boasted an armament of unimaginable firepower,<ref name="On the Front Lines">''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]''</ref> composed of over 5,000 turbolasers,<ref name="Rebel Files" /> including 750 twin heavy turbolaser batteries, and 1000 turret-mounted twin light turbolaser batteries. The ''Executor''-class Dreadnought additionally possessed 125 assault [[concussion missile launcher]]s, 100 twin battleship ion cannons and 250 turret-mounted [[quad laser cannon]]s.<ref name="Starships and Speeders" />

===Complement===
[[File:ReaperStarDestroyer.jpg|thumb|left|200px|An ''Executor''-class Dreadnought with several ''Imperial''-class Star Destroyers]]
The ''Executor''-class Dreadnought had a complement of over 1,000 starships,<ref name="Starfighters" /> including 144 [[TIE series|TIE Series]] starfighters, divided into 12 [[squadron]]s. The ''Executor''-class Dreadnought's TIEs were composed of [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE/ln fighters]], [[TIE/sa tactical bomber|TIE/sa bombers]] and [[TIE/IN interceptor]]s.<ref name="UltimateSW" /> The ''Executor''-class Dreadnought also possessed 200 assault [[shuttle]]s, transport shuttles, and support craft, and [[Y-85 Titan dropship]]s.<ref name="CL2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> As well as its space complement, the ''Executor''-class Dreadnought carried several [[AT-series|All Terrain]] [[walker]]s included 24 [[All Terrain Armored Transport|AT-ATs]] and 50 [[All Terrain Scout Transport|AT-STs]], and 2 [[IM-455 modular garrison/Canon|IM-455 modular garrisons]]<ref name="Starships and Speeders" />

==History==
{{Quote|Can you imagine what the twenty-two I've saved would add to the ''Chimaera's'' defenses? Or the ''Firedrake's'', or the new ''Star Dreadnought'' class Lord Vader's been pushing for?|Grand Admiral [[Balanhai Savit]], on the resources he'd stolen from the Death Star project, to Grand Admiral [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]]|<ref name="Thrawn: Treason">''[[Thrawn: Treason]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Eclipse_Executor-class_SWA.png|thumb|right|250px|The ''Eclipse'' bombards a planet.]]
The ''Executor''-class Star Dreadnought, also known as the ''Super''-class Star Destroyer,<ref name="VE" /> was manufactured by [[Kuat Drive Yards]] during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Starfighters" /> By the [[time]] of the [[skirmish against the Third Fleet]], [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] had been pushing for the class.<ref name="Thrawn: Treason" /> During its history, at least two prototypes were manufactured, including the [[Star Dreadnought Assault Prototype]] and the [[Star Dreadnought Command Prototype]].<ref name="Announcement">{{FantasyFlightGames|url=en/news/2018/8/3/executor-arrives|text=Executor Arrives}}</ref> With the massive amount of resources taken up by the [[Project Stardust|Death Star project]],<ref name="Darth Vader (2015) 2" /> development of the ''Executor''-class was held back.<ref name="Thrawn: Treason" />

The [[Liberty's Misrule|''Annihilator'']] served as [[Grand General]] [[Cassio Tagge]]'s [[flagship]]<ref name="Darth Vader (2015) 2" /> before he prepared to move his command to an under-construction ''Executor''-class, known simply as the ''[[Executor]]''.<ref name="Darth Vader (2015) 20">[[Darth Vader (2015) 20|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 20]]</ref> Tagge was a fierce critic of the Death Star, pointing out that countless Super Star Destroyers could have been made with the resources thrown into the single [[battle station]].<ref name="Darth Vader (2015) 2" /> Upon seeing the ''Executor'', Vader's personal [[assassin droid]]s, [[0-0-0]] and [[BT-1]], debated whether the massive vessel was "trashy," with 0-0-0 admitting he would like an ''Executor''-class of his own.<ref name="Darth Vader (2015) 20" /> After Tagge's failings allowed the rogue [[scientist]] [[Cylo]] to [[Cylo Hijacking|nearly commandeer]] the ''Executor'', [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] gave command of the vessel and Tagge's fleet to Vader, who executed Tagge shortly after.<ref name="Darth Vader (2015) 25">[[Darth Vader (2015) 25|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 25]]</ref>

[[File:SW_Executor_01.jpg|thumb|left|220px|The ''Executor'' was a well known ''Executor''-class Star Dreadnought.]]
According to the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance's]] [[Rebel Alliance Intelligence Service|intelligence agency]], more than a dozen [[Super Star Destroyer]]s were made, including the ''Executor'' itself, its sister ship the ''[[Lusankya]]'', [[Oppressor (Executor-class)|''Oppressor'']], the ''Annihilator'', the ''[[Arbitrator]]'', the [[Eclipse (Executor-class)|''Eclipse'']], and the ''[[Ravager]]''. However, the true number remained a subject of debate, as Alliance analysts endeavored to make sense of Imperial [[propaganda]] and see through the black budgets designed to hide the scope of the Palpatine's secret weapons programs.<ref name="CL 2016" /> As Vader's flagship, the ''Executor'' saw action at the [[Battle of Mako-Ta]]<ref name="Star Wars 50" /> in [[1 ABY]],<ref name="1 ABY Date">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]'' states that the Assault on the [[Mako-Ta Space Docks]] took place twenty [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Proclamation of the New Order|formation]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[19 BBY]]. Therefore, the assault must have taken place in [[1 ABY]].</ref> the [[Battle of Hoth]] and the [[Escape from Cloud City]]<ref name="Episode V">{{Film|V}}</ref> in [[3 ABY]],<ref name="TESB Date">{{FilmDate|V}}</ref> and the [[Attack on the Executor|battle over Jekara]] during the [[War of the Bounty Hunters]].<ref name="WOTBH 5">[[War of the Bounty Hunters 5|''War of the Bounty Hunters'' 5]]</ref> It was destroyed at the [[Battle of Endor]] in [[4 ABY]].<ref name="On the Front Lines">''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]''</ref>

In the months after the events of [[Endor]], the [[New Republic]], the successor government to the Alliance, destroyed five Super Star Destroyers, including the ''Arbitrator'' which accidentally jumped into a black hole due to erroneous hyperspace coordinates, and captured three more. The ''Annihilator'', former flagship of Grand General Cassio Tagge, was captured by pirates and renamed ''Liberty's Misrule''. The only known Super Star Destroyer, and so the only known ''Executor''-class, to remain in Imperial hands was [[Grand Admiral]] [[Rae Sloane]]'s flagship ''Ravager'', which also served as the base for [[Fleet Admiral]] [[Gallius Rax]].<ref name="Life Debt" /> In [[5 ABY]],<ref name="Life Debt Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]'' to [[5 ABY]].</ref> Sloane discovered evidence that the Emperor's command ship, the Super Star Destroyer ''Eclipse'', had not been destroyed but had vanished from the official records.<ref name="Life Debt" />

[[File:SSD-SWE.png|thumb|right|220px|Dorsal view of the ''Executor'']]
Following Sloane's disappearance during the [[attack on Chandrila]], Fleet Admiral Rax formally took command of the ''Ravager'' as [[Counselor to the Empire]]. The ''Ravager'' then rendezvoused with a large Imperial armada on the barren planet of [[Jakku]] for a showdown with the New Republic.<ref name="Life Debt" /> The ''Ravager'' was lost in the [[Battle of Jakku|battle]] when one of the New Republic's [[Starhawk-class battleship|''Starhawk''-class battleships]] pulled it into Jakku's gravity well with its ultra-powerful tractor beam, causing the massive capital ship to crash in the sands of the desert planet.<ref name="CL 2016" />

